# Build context excludes for `podman build -f os/Containerfile .` (context = repo
# root). The multi-stage builder COPYs the whole workspace source; everything
# here is either huge, regenerated in-image, or irrelevant to the build — and a
# stray `target/` (tens of GB after local builds) makes the COPY OOM/hang.

# Rust build output (the in-image build uses its own cache mounts, not this).
target/
**/target/

# VCS + tooling
.git/
**/.git
.claude/

# Image build outputs
os/output*/
os/external-assets/cache/

# Stale host-built binaries (the multi-stage build compiles in-image now;
# these are leftovers from the old host-build flow and must not shadow it).
os/shell
os/fs
os/terminal
os/file-explorer
os/tilo-greeter
os/tilo-installer
os/browser
# build-custom-installer.sh assembles this one-shot overlay in a temporary
# context; it is a declared staged input for Containerfile.installer, not a
# directory that belongs in the repository build context.
os/rootfs/

# Logs / scratch
*.log
**/*.h264

# Keep Cargo.lock — needed for a reproducible resolve in the builder stage.

# The Containerfiles themselves. podman reads them via -f, from the filesystem, so
# they never need to be IN the context — and while they were, editing one
# invalidated the builder stage's `COPY . /build` and re-ran the whole Rust compile
# to fix a typo in a step near the end.
os/Containerfile
os/Containerfile.*
